tus":"p","title":"Big Data, Surveillance and Crisis Management"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c116e67a-db25-4d95-b59a-17344c0b6e75"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Triggering Action: Participatory Surveillance and Event Detection in Public Emergency Management","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384085","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"From smartphones, meters, fridges and cars to internet platforms, the data of digital technologies are the data of citizens. In addition to raising political and ethical issues of privacy, confidentiality and data protection, this calls for rethinking relations to citizens in the production of data for statistics if they are to be trusted by citizens. We outline an approach that involves co-producing data with citizens as partners of statistical production, from the design of a data production platform to the interpretation and analysis of data. While raising issues such as data quality and reliability, we argue co-production can potentially mitigate problems associated with the re-purposing of Big Data. We argue that in a time of “alternative facts”, what constitutes legitimate knowledge and expertise are major political sites of contention and struggle and require going beyond defending existing practices towards inventing new ones. In this context, we contend that the future of official statistics not only depends on inventing new data sources and methods but also mobilising the possibilities of digital technologies to establish new relations with citizens.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ruppert, Evelyn","Grommé, Francisca","Ustek-Spilda, Funda","Cakici, Baki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383063"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Goldsmiths, University of London","The London School of Economics and Political Science"],"keyword":["Citizen science","Co production","Experimentalism","Privacy by Design","smart statistics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"citizen data and trust in official statistics","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.24187/ecostat.2018.505d.1971","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383063","identifier":[{"id":"85066838829","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7a07bf21-4832-45cc-9381-65c36be41d07"],"keyword":["citizen science","co‑production","experimentalism","privacy‑by‑design","smart statistics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-DC619BF04861339EFE6EDC0455AEA659"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.24187/ecostat.2018.505d.1971","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84195222/505_506_Ruppert_Gromme_Ustek_Spilda_Cakici_EN.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"goldsmiths university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Goldsmiths, University of London","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"the london school of economics and political science","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"The London School of Economics and Political Science","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Evelyn","key":"ruppertpau","last":"Ruppert","name":"Ruppert, Evelyn","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Francisca","key":"grommépau","last":"Grommé","name":"Grommé, Francisca","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Funda","key":"ustekspildapau","last":"Ustek-Spilda","name":"Ustek-Spilda, Funda","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Baki","key":"cakicipau","last":"Cakici","locid":"b614ac6f-eefa-44a3-8b9a-092b88d86d37","name":"Cakici, Baki","orcid":"0000-0002-1039-8177","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.24187/ecostat.2018.505d.1971","issn":["17775574"],"issue":"505-506","journal":"Economie et Statistique / Economics and Statistics","pages":"171","publisher":"Institut national de la statistique et des études économiques","status":"p","title":"Economie et Statistique / Economics and Statistics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85066838829"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7a07bf21-4832-45cc-9381-65c36be41d07"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Citizen Data and Trust in Official Statistics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383063","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This working paper was written in preparation for a collaborative workshop organised for statisticians, social scientists, information and app designers and other participants inside and outside academia. The autumn 2017 workshop aimed to develop the main principles for a citizen data app for official statistics. Through this work we sought to conceive of a new regime of data collection in official statistics through different devices. How can we capture citizens’ meanings and intentions when they produce data? Can we develop ‘smart’ methods that do not rely on cooperating with, and data generated by, large tech companies, but by developing methods and data co-produced with citizens? Towards addressing these issues we developed four key concepts outlined in this document: experimentalism, citizen data, smart statistics and privacy by design. We introduced these concepts to facilitate shared understandings of their meaning, provide a background to discussions about them and the questions they raise for official statistics. Through then jointly working on the practical development of a citizen data app, the objective was to reflect on and reshape these concepts and to identify other concepts that might aid our understanding of the possibilities of citizen co-production of data for official statistics.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Grommé, Francisca","Ustek, Funda","Ruppert, Evelyn","Cakici, Baki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382838"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Citizen Data","Data Co Production","Official Statistics","Privacy by Design","Smart Methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"citizen data and official statistics background document to a collaborative workshop","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"http://research.gold.ac.uk/20740/1/ARITHMUS%20collaborative%20workshop%20wp_final%20version%20060717.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382838","ids":["itu-68f239d5-8d89-491d-b962-da0733fbc220"],"keyword":["Citizen Data","Data Co-Production","Official Statistics","Privacy by Design","Smart Methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E57FA41BF837EB79A69805C07A11900A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"http://research.gold.ac.uk/20740/1/ARITHMUS%20collaborative%20workshop%20wp_final%20version%20060717.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Francisca","key":"grommépau","last":"Grommé","name":"Grommé, Francisca","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Funda","key":"ustekpau","last":"Ustek","name":"Ustek, Funda","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Evelyn","key":"ruppertpau","last":"Ruppert","name":"Ruppert, Evelyn","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Baki","key":"cakicipau","last":"Cakici","locid":"b614ac6f-eefa-44a3-8b9a-092b88d86d37","name":"Cakici, Baki","orcid":"0000-0002-1039-8177","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"place":"London, UK","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","