S01-000.00-383820","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Information and communication technologies are not value-neutral tools that reflect reality; they privilege some forms of action, and they limit others. We analyze reports describing the design, development, testing and evaluation of a European Commission co-funded syndromic surveillance project called SIDARTHa (System for Information on Detection and Analysis of Risks and Threats to Health). We show that the reports construct the concept of a health threat as a sudden, unexpected event with the potential to cause severe harm and one that requires a public health response aided by surveillance. Based on our analysis, we state that when creating surveillance technologies, design choices have consequences for what can be seen and for what remains invisible. Finally, we argue that syndromic surveillance discourse privileges expertise in developing, maintaining and using software within public health practice, and it prioritizes standardized and transportable knowledge over local and context-dependent knowledge. We conclude that syndromic surveillance contributes to a shift in broader public health practice, with consequences for fairness if design choices and prioritizations remain invisible and unchallenged.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Cakici, Baki","Sanches, Pedro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382900"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Swedish Institute of Computer Science"],"keyword":["Discourse","Epidemiology","ICT","Public Health Surveillance","Syndromic surveillance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"detecting the visible the discursive construction of health threats in a syndromic surveillance system design","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/soc4030399","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382900","identifier":[{"id":"84977942960","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6dca92c3-efb2-4527-8b29-1e91298789a4"],"keyword":["ICT","discourse","epidemiology","public health surveillance","syndromic surveillance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6E5910E9C3CF3A10B04ABEB33F4E47AF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/soc4030399","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"swedish institute of computer science","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Swedish Institute of Computer Science","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Baki","key":"cakicipau","last":"Cakici","name":"Cakici, Baki","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"sanchespau","last":"Sanches","name":"Sanches, Pedro","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/soc4030399","issn":["20754698"],"issue":"3","journal":"Societies","pages":"399-413","publisher":"MDPI","status":"p","title":"Societies","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6dca92c3-efb2-4527-8b29-1e91298789a4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Detecting the Visible: The Discursive Construction of Health Threats in a Syndromic Surveillance System Design","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382900","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, I examine design documents from three different ICT design and development projects. I argue that they present intersecting visions of sustainability entailing the wide-spread use of ICT, describe the properties of users compatible with such ICT, and provide ways of judging the users. In the design documents, the inhabitants are made individually responsible for living sustainably, and surveillance is positioned as integral to this future with the help of ICT. Underlying the visions, I identify a translation process that captures the traces of the inhabitants’ lives, classifies them according to different criteria of sustainable living, and returns them to the tapestry of everyday life to convince the users to behave differently. In the discourses of these documents, surveillance translates the traces, and the translations exert new pressures on existing power relations.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Cakici, Baki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381843"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stockholm University"],"keyword":["ICT Design and Development","Power Relations in Technology","Sustainability","Translation process","User Surveillance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sustainability through surveillance ict discourses in design documents","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82245703/Cakici_2013_Sustainability_Through_Surveillance_ICT_Discourse.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381843","identifier":[{"id":"84881280568","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-260162f6-6520-4097-bbf6-7396e32215c9"],"keyword":["ICT Design and Development","Power Relations in Technology","Sustainability","Translation Process","User Surveillance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B4E28ABDB91F8F14A635845C81BDCA06"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82245703/Cakici_2013_Sustainability_Through_Surveillance_ICT_Discourse.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"stockholm university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm University","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Baki","key":"cakicipau","last":"Cakici","name":"Cakici, Baki","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["14777487"],"issue":"1/2","journal":"Surveillance and Society","pages":"177-189","publisher":"Surveillance Studies Network","status":"p","title":"Surveillance and Society","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-260162f6-6520-4097-bbf6-7396e32215c9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Sustainability Through Surveillance: ICT Discourses in Design Documents","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381843","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"A critical investigation into computational models developed for studying the spread of communicable disease is presented. The case in point is a spatially explicit micro–meso–macro model for the entire Swedish population built on registry data, thus far used for smallpox and for influenza-like illnesses. The lessons learned from a software development project of more than 100 person months are collected into a check list. The list is intended for use by computational epidemiologists and policy makers, and the workflow incorporating these two roles is described in detail.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Cakici, Baki","Boman, Magnus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381356"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Computational epidemiology","Individual based simulation","Policy making","Workflow"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a workflow for software development within computational epidemiology","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jocs.2011.05.004","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381356","identifier":[{"id":"80052883032","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-0677d77d-a134-4c4d-a152-8d35f77c64f5"],"keyword":["Computational epidemiology","Individual-based simulation","Policy making","Workflow"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1A4B0C6930B21547BBAE933622418836"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jocs.2011.05.004","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Baki","key":"cakicipau","last":"Cakici","name":"Cakici, Baki","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Magnus","key":"bomanpau","last":"Boman","name":"Boman, Magnus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jocs.2011.05.004","issn":["18777503"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Computational Science","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Computational Science","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0677d77d-a134-4c4d-a152-8d35f77c64f5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Workflow for Software Development Within Computational Epidemiology","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381356","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
